Pooled CRISPR screen data of {{ samples | length }} samples were analysed with
the crispr-screens workflow {{ workflow_version }}
(https://github.com/niekwit/crispr-screens) in {{ tool("snakemake") }}.

## Read processing and sgRNA counts

{% if cram %}
Reads were extracted from CRAM files with {{ tool("samtools", "samtools fastq") }}.
{% endif %}
Read quality was assessed with {{ tool("fastqc") }} before and after
trimming, and the reports were combined with {{ tool("multiqc") }}. Reads were
trimmed with {{ tool("cutadapt", code(cutadapt_extra)) }}. The sgRNA sequences
of the library ({{ library_name }}: {{ n_sgrnas | number }} sgRNAs targeting
{{ n_genes | number }} genes) were indexed with bowtie-build, and the trimmed
reads were aligned to them with {{ tool("bowtie", code(bowtie_extra)) }}.
Aligned reads were counted per sgRNA; sgRNAs without aligned reads were given
a count of 0.

Quality control included alignment rates, read numbers, fold coverage of the
library, sgRNAs without reads, read count distributions, the evenness of sgRNA
representation (Gini index and the ratio of the 90th to the 10th percentile of
the counts), Pearson correlation of log-transformed counts between samples, and
a principal component analysis of log2(count + 1) with
{{ tool("scikit-learn") }}.

{% if crisprcleanr_comparisons %}
{% set ccr_uses = [] %}
{% if bagel2 %}{% set _ = ccr_uses.append("BAGEL2") %}{% endif %}
{% if rra and mageck["apply_crisprcleanr"] %}{% set _ = ccr_uses.append("MAGeCK") %}{% endif %}
{% if drugz and st["drugz"]["apply_crisprcleanr"] %}{% set _ = ccr_uses.append("DrugZ") %}{% endif %}
## Correction of gene-independent responses

Before analysis with {{ ccr_uses | join_and }}, gene-independent responses to CRISPR–Cas9
targeting were corrected per comparison
({{ crisprcleanr_comparisons | join_and }}) with {{ tool("crisprcleanr") }}.
Counts of the test and control samples were normalised and sgRNA log fold
changes calculated, removing sgRNAs with few reads in the control sample(s)
(ccr.NormfoldChanges, {{ code("min_reads = " ~ ccr["min_reads"]) }}). The fold
changes, averaged over the test samples, were ordered by the genomic position
of the sgRNAs (from
{% if ccr["library_name"] in ccr_libraries %}
the CRISPRcleanR annotation of {{ ccr["library_name"] }}
{% else %}
the library file
{% endif %}
) and corrected (ccr.GWclean), and corrected counts were calculated
(ccr.correctCounts, {{ code("minTargetedGenes = 3") }}). The separation of
{% if essential == "none" and non_essential == "none" %}
reference essential and non-essential genes {{ cite("hart2016") }}
{% else %}
{% if essential != "none" %}
the essential genes in {{ essential }}
{% else %}
reference essential genes {{ cite("hart2016") }}
{% endif %}
and
{% if non_essential != "none" %}
the non-essential genes in {{ non_essential }}
{% else %}
reference non-essential genes {{ cite("hart2016") }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
by the corrected fold changes was assessed with ROC and precision-recall
curves (ccr.ROC_Curve and ccr.PrRc_Curve).
{% endif %}

