## MAGeCK

{% set options = (mageck_control ~ " " ~ mageck_extra).split() | join(" ") %}
{% if rra %}
Enriched and depleted genes of each comparison ({{ comparisons | join_and }})
were identified with {{ tool("mageck", "test, robust rank aggregation") }}
{% if mageck["apply_crisprcleanr"] %}
from the CRISPRcleanR-corrected counts, without further normalisation
{% elif "--norm-method" not in options %}
from the counts, after median normalisation
{% else %}
from the counts
{% endif %}
{% else %}
Gene effects (beta scores) were estimated with
{{ tool("mageck", "mle, " ~ citation("li2015")) }} from the counts of the
samples of each design matrix ({{ matrices | join_and }})
{% if "--norm-method" not in options %}
, after median normalisation
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if options %}
, with {{ code(options) }}
{% endif %}
.
{% if cnv %}
Copy-number bias was corrected with MAGeCK's CNV correction
({{ code("--cnv-norm --cell-line " ~ mageck["cell_line"]) }};
{{ citation("wang2019") }}), using the gene-level copy numbers of the Cancer
Cell Line Encyclopedia (2013-12-03 release; {{ citation("barretina2012") }}).
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if drugz %}
## DrugZ

Chemogenetic interactions in each comparison ({{ comparisons | join_and }})
were scored with
{{ tool("drugz", code(st["drugz"]["extra"]) if st["drugz"]["extra"] else None) }}
{% if st["drugz"]["apply_crisprcleanr"] %}
from the CRISPRcleanR-corrected counts.
{% else %}
from the counts.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if bagel2 %}
## BAGEL2

Gene essentiality in each comparison ({{ comparisons_bagel2 | join_and }}) was
scored with {{ tool("bagel2") }}: Bayes factors from the CRISPRcleanR-corrected
fold changes (BAGEL.py bf
{%- if st["bagel2"]["extra_args"]["bf"] %}, {{ code(st["bagel2"]["extra_args"]["bf"]) }}{% endif %}
) and precision and recall (BAGEL.py pr
{%- if st["bagel2"]["extra_args"]["pr"] %}, {{ code(st["bagel2"]["extra_args"]["pr"]) }}{% endif %}
), with
{% set human = config["lib_info"]["species"] == "human" %}
{% if essential == "none" and non_essential == "none" and not human %}
the mouse reference essential and non-essential genes distributed with BAGEL2
{% else %}
{% if essential != "none" %}
the essential genes in {{ essential }}
{% elif human %}
the reference core essential genes CEGv2 {{ cite("hart2017") }}
{% else %}
the mouse reference essential genes distributed with BAGEL2
{% endif %}
and
{% if non_essential != "none" %}
the non-essential genes in {{ non_essential }}
{% elif human %}
the reference non-essential genes NEGv1 {{ cite("hart2014") }}
{% else %}
the mouse reference non-essential genes distributed with BAGEL2
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
.
{% endif %}

{% if string_db["run"] and string_db_queries %}
{% set top = string_db["top_genes"] %}
{% set fdr = string_db["fdr"] %}
{% set data = string_db["data"] %}
{% set directions = {"both": "enriched and depleted genes (separately)",
  "enriched": "enriched genes", "depleted": "depleted genes"}[data] %}
{% set beta = {"both": "genes with beta > 0 and with beta < 0 (separately)",
  "enriched": "genes with beta > 0", "depleted": "genes with beta < 0"}[data] %}
{% set ranked = (["MAGeCK"] if rra else []) + (["DrugZ"] if drugz else []) %}
{% set sets = [] %}
{% if ranked and top > 0 %}
{% set _ = sets.append("the top " ~ top ~ " " ~ directions ~ " of each "
  ~ join_and(ranked) ~ " comparison, ranked by " ~ join_and(ranked, " or ")
  ~ " rank") %}
{% elif ranked %}
{% set _ = sets.append("the " ~ directions ~ " with FDR < " ~ fdr ~ " of each "
  ~ join_and(ranked) ~ " comparison") %}
{% endif %}
{% if mle and top > 0 %}
{% set _ = sets.append("the top " ~ top ~ " " ~ beta
  ~ " of each MAGeCK MLE condition, ranked by FDR") %}
{% elif mle %}
{% set _ = sets.append("the " ~ beta ~ " with FDR < " ~ fdr
  ~ " of each MAGeCK MLE condition") %}
{% endif %}
{% if bagel2 and top > 0 %}
{% set _ = sets.append("the top " ~ top
  ~ " genes of each BAGEL2 comparison, ranked by Bayes factor") %}
{% elif bagel2 %}
{% set _ = sets.append("the genes with a Bayes factor > " ~ string_db["bf_cutoff"]
  ~ " of each BAGEL2 comparison") %}
{% endif %}
## Functional enrichment

Functional enrichment was tested with {{ tool("string") }}, queried through
its API ({{ config["lib_info"]["species"] }}, NCBI taxon {{ taxon }}) on
{{ package_version("string-db-date") }}, for {{ sets | join("; ") }}. Terms
with an FDR < 0.05 (as reported by STRING) were kept, and the STRING network
of the genes was drawn.
